.TH EUCLID-CLI-ENS-LIST-TOPICS 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.18.37" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ens-list-topics \- list notification topics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli ens list-topics
[\fB\-\-prefix\fR|\fB\-p\fR \fIPREFIX\fR]
[\fB\-\-pageSize\fR|\fB\-s\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-pageIndex\fR|\fB\-i\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-sortColumn\fR|\fB\-c\fR \fICOLUMN\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists topics in the caller's own account, optionally filtered by name
prefix and paginated.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-prefix " " \fIPREFIX\fR
Only list topics whose name starts with this prefix. Optional; if
omitted, all topics in the account are listed.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-pageSize " " \fIN\fR
Maximum number of topics to return. Defaults to \fI-1\fR (no paging).
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-pageIndex " " \fIN\fR
Zero-based page index to return when \fB\-\-pageSize\fR is set.
Defaults to \fI-1\fR.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-sortColumn " " \fICOLUMN\fR
Column to sort results by. Defaults to \fIname\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The matching topics are printed as JSON (possibly an empty list).
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, or the
server rejected the request.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ens list-topics

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ens list-topics \e
    --prefix order- --pageSize 20 --pageIndex 0 --sortColumn name
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-ens (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-create-topic (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-get-topic-ern (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-list-messages (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-delete-topic (1)
